Paper presentation round 2: Figure 1 with results panels, appendix A-L rewritten, captions self-contained, audit fixes

- Figure 1: a fourth part, "What we find", with three bar panels and 95% intervals (read set vs
  dependency set; B x D by item class after S_def; check-only vs D=0 and what the authored
  derivation adds); the orphan branch is marked; the old figure's "+15.2 pp against D=0" is
  corrected to "over the check-only cell".
- Main text: one name per concept (authored derivation, check-only cell, orphan branch, oracle key,
  blanket refresh, add-only refresh, item-time, diagnostic tests); Section 5 headings are claims and
  no sentence carries more than four numbers; the class-split table becomes Figure 2; Section 6 is a
  Discussion with numbered design rules; abstract leads with the finding.
- Fixed facts and references: the check-only cell is exploratory (logged before it ran), not
  registered; T1 holds in 5 of 8 switches, 2 of the 5 to other writers; the M1 difference has the
  printed sign; +76.2 pp is labelled as repair correctness over all re-derived definition items;
  four appendix pointers corrected; baselines stated for +15.2/+31.4 pp, the pooled oracle-key gain
  and the Holm family.
- Appendix: twelve sections A-L, each opening with what it supports; deviations as one table; the
  neighbour table is the self-contained full version; misses and JSON-arm tables sit with their
  text; 27 appendix pages, 49 in all, main text ends on page 12.
- Generators: self-contained captions; one interval format est [lo, hi]; key-audit field totals;
  native-null out-of-sample baselines and total row; mechanistic repair, P- IDs with their arms,
  deletion-aware; audit-table owner column; "replication" instead of a bare R; left-aligned table
  notes, right-aligned difference columns. numbers.tex is byte-identical.

